orm to strip everything from `package.json` except for\nthe `\"version\"` field.\n\nInstallation\n----\n\n    npm install --save package-json-versionify\n\nDescription\n----\n\nSay you want to ship a library, and do something like:\n\n```js\nMyLibrary.version = require('./package.json').version;\n```\n\nUnfortunately, if you do this, then your entire `package.json` will be included\nin the output Browserify bundle, which will increase your bundle size. Bummer!\n\nHowever, if you use this transform, then it will remove everything from `package.json` except for the `\"version\"` field. So when you `require('./package.json')`, you get something much more compact, e.g.:\n\n```js\n{\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}\n```\n","maintainers":[{"name":"nolanlawson","email":"nolan@nolanlawson.com"}],"time":{"modified":"2022-06-23T06:35:07.544Z","created":"2015-12-25T19:27:30.388Z","1.0.0":"2015-12-25T19:27:30.388Z","1.0.1":"2016-01-15T02:49:34.466Z","1.0.2":"2016-02-20T16:34:28.355Z","1.0.3":"2016-11-03T16:31:32.132Z","1.0.4":"2016-12-22T01:46:57.218Z"},"keywords":[],"author":{"name":"Nolan Lawson","email":"nolan@nolanlawson.com"},"license":"Apache-2.0","readmeFilename":"README.md","homepage":"https://github.com/nolanlawson/package-json-versionify#readme","repository":{"type":"git","url":"git+https://github.com/nolanlawson/package-json-versionify.git"},"bugs":{"url":"https://github.com/nolanlawson/package-json-versionify/issues"},"users":{"antoniopf":true}}